### 1. Preliminaries  

> “For a fixed integer \(n\ge3\) define  
> \[
> T_n=\{(a,b)\in\mathbb Z_{>0}^2\mid a+b\le n+1\}.
> \]  
> … A simple count gives  
> \[
> |T_n|=\sum_{a=1}^{n}(n+1-a)=\frac{n(n+1)}2 .
> \tag{1}
> \]”

**Verification:**  
The set \(T_n\) is exactly the lattice points in the right‑angled triangle with vertices \((1,1),(n,1),(1,n)\). For each \(a\) (the \(x\)-coordinate) there are \(n+1-a\) admissible \(b\)’s, so the sum is \(\sum_{a=1}^{n}(n+1-a)=1+2+\dots +n=n(n+1)/2\). The computation is correct.  

**Conclusion:** Correct.

