**Verification:**  
All algebraic steps are correct. The reduction to a slope \(p/q\) with \((p,q)=1\) is standard. The deduction that the sum \(x+y\) changes by \((p+q)t\) is accurate, giving the arithmetic‑progression claim. Since the admissible sums satisfy \(2\le x+y\le n+1\), the bound (3) follows directly. The observation that a sunny line cannot be vertical, hence can intersect any fixed column in at most one point, is also correct.  

