### 1.  Reduction to the triangle \(T_k\)

> “Replace each non‑sunny line by a vertical line that passes through the leftmost column not yet occupied by a vertical line. A vertical line covers **all** points of a column, whereas a horizontal line or a line of slope $-1$ can meet a column in at most one point. Hence after the replacement we still cover every point of $S_n$ and we have exactly the same number $k$ of sunny lines.”

*Correctness of the idea.*  
If a non‑sunny line is horizontal or of slope $-1$, it indeed meets any fixed column in at most one lattice point, while a vertical line meets the whole column. Replacing a non‑sunny line by a vertical line therefore **cannot decrease** the number of points covered in that column.

